Track 3: The Cycle Survived the Power Cut
- Story & Context: During a small mesh session, the temporary electrical supply trips while the band is in the middle of its densest section. The dub mixer, bass amplifier, and guitar rig disappear instantly, but the acoustic mbira continues without interruption. Audience members stop moving, and Leon begins tapping the unamplified guitar body instead of playing strings.

Rehema joins with breath-only flute sounds while Tawanda uses the metal edge of the dead amplifier as percussion. The power returns after several minutes, but the band chooses not to restore the previous arrangement. Instead, Tawanda brings back only one sub pulse and a single delay send, allowing the electronic system to re-enter around the acoustic cycle rather than reclaim control.

The recorded version preserves the exact silence at the moment of the outage and the low hum when power returns. The emotional center is continuity: the composition does not need the grid to survive.
